:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/316"} "Deutschlandhalle, Berlin"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/22107"} "24 from 24 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single elimination tournament."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The welterweight division had no clear favorite, although the German fighter " [:a {:href "/athletes/3631"} "Michael Murach"] " was expected to perform well in front of a home audience. " [:a {:href "/athletes/3820"} "Imre Mándi"] " of Hungary and " [:a {:href "/athletes/5038"} "Rusty Cook"] " of Australia were also expected to put in strong performances."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Mándi’s victory over the US boxer " [:a {:href "/athletes/8761"} "Chester Rutecki"] " was hotly disputed by the American team management, as Mándi hit the canvas in the first round and was warned for fouling on four occasions, but won the decision. US boxing coach Johnny Behr was quoted as saying, “This beats the Olympic record for terrible decisions”. The US boxing team withdrew from the Olympics, only to reconsider their decision an hour later."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Another controversy occurred in the very first bout of the competition. When Uruguay’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/8583"} "Francisco Costanzo"] " was disqualified in his match against " [:a {:href "/athletes/3105"} "Roger Tritz"] " of France, his supporters surrounded the ring and threatened to slit the referee’s throat."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Finland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/2973"} "Sten Suvio"] " was not blessed with an easy draw. He faced Cook and Mándi in successive rounds, but managed to gain the decision over both. After a semi-final victory over the eventual bronze medal winner, " [:a {:href "/athletes/1754"} "Gerhard Pedersen"] " of Denmark, he found himself facing Murach in the final. Very much the outsider in the final, Suvio bided his time in the first three minutes as Murach launched his attacks. Suvio’s opportunity came halfway through the second round, and a hard right hand stopped the German in his tracks and changed the course of the fight. The Finn began to dominate, landing punch after punch, and Murach briefly visited the canvas as he tired badly. Suvio’s victory was the first gold medal victory by a Finnish boxer."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Michael Murach went on to defeat Mándi in the final of the 1937 European Championship, but was to die fighting on the Eastern Front in 1941. Sven Suvio fought in the Finnish army but survived to resume his modestly successful career as a professional. " [:a {:href "/athletes/4999"} "Raúl Rodríguez"] " of Argentina, who lost in the last eight, became professional middleweight champion of South America."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/2973"} "Sten Suvio"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FIN.png"}] "FIN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/3631"} "Michael Murach"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/1754"} "Gerhard Pedersen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/DEN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/DEN.png"}] "DEN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/3105"} "Roger Trit